<pre><h1>                       Exercise Name: Incline Push-Up</h1></pre>
    <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>
    Target Muscle Activation

 Primary: Lower & Mid Chest / Pectorals (~65%)
 Secondary: Triceps Brachii (~35%) & Anterior Deltoids (Shoulders)

</div></div>


<h1>Step-by-Step Execution Guide</h1>

<u><b><h4>1. Setup:</h4></b></u>
 Place your hands on an elevated platform (like a stable box, bench, or step) slightly wider than shoulder-width apart.
 Step your feet back until your legs and body are fully extended, forming a straight line from your head to your heels.
 Engage your core and glutes to prevent your hips from sagging.


<u><b><h4>2. The Descent (Eccentric Phase):</h4></b></u>
 Inhale and lower your chest toward the edge of the box by bending your elbows.
 Keep your elbows tucked at roughly a 45-degree angle to your torso (avoid flaring them out wide).
 Lower yourself until your lower chest lightly touches or nearly touches the box edge.


<u><b><h4>3. The Push (Concentric Phase):</h4></b></u>
 Exhale and press firmly through your palms to extend your arms back to the starting plank position.
 Lock out your arms in a controlled manner without rounding your back.




<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Beginner-Friendly:</b> Elevating your upper body reduces gravitational force, making push-ups accessible if standard floor push-ups are too challenging.<br>
 
 <b>◉Lower Chest Focus:</b> Changing the angle shifts emphasis slightly toward the lower portion of the pectoral muscles.<br>
 
 <b>◉ Reduced Joint Stress:</b> Places less pressure on the wrists, elbows, and shoulders compared to flat or decline variations.<br>
 
 <b>◉ Versatile Finishing Move:</b> Advanced lifters can use incline push-ups at the end of a chest workout to push their muscles to failure safely.



<h1>Recommended Sets & Repetitions</h1>

 Beginner Progression: 3 sets of 8–12 reps.
 Hypertrophy & Toning: 3–4 sets of 12–15 reps.
 High-Volume Endurance / Burn-out: 3 sets of 15–25 reps (or to muscle failure).
 Rest: 60 seconds between sets.

